// Scene Size: 20
// Scene Grid: 10
// AI geometry tool-use demo — Proof-Carrying Clearance
//
// The certify tool PROVES a geometric claim over a WHOLE region with interval
// arithmetic — a sound verdict, not a sampled guess, and with no Lipschitz
// constant to get wrong. When a claim fails, certify returns a counterexample
// box to repair toward. Open the AI chat and give it this task.
//
// TRY THIS PROMPT:
//   Seat the peg inside the bracket's pocket — centered, resting clear of the
//   walls and floor. Then PROVE the placement with the certify tool over a
//   region containing both: (1) the peg does not interfere with the bracket
//   anywhere — certify max(peg, bracket) >= 0; and (2) it clears the bracket by
//   at least 1 mm everywhere — certify max(peg, bracket) >= 0.5 (the separation
//   is twice the minimum). If certify DISPROVES a claim it returns a
//   counterexample box — move the peg to fix it and certify again. Return the
//   seated peg and report what you proved.
//
// What to watch: certify comes back proven / disproven (with a counterexample
// box) / indeterminate. A proven verdict holds EVERYWHERE in the region, not
// just at the points the model happened to sample — the guarantee extremum's
// caller-supplied Lipschitz constant and grid sampling can't give.

box(x1, y1, z1, x2, y2, z2) {
  return max(
    x1 - p.x, p.x - x2,
    y1 - p.y, p.y - y2,
    z1 - p.z, p.z - z2,
  );
}

// Bracket: a solid block with a square pocket open at the top (floor 1 mm thick).
bracketOuter = box(-15.0, -15.0, 0.0, 15.0, 15.0, 12.0);
pocket = box(-8.0, -8.0, 1.0, 8.0, 8.0, 13.0);
bracket = max(bracketOuter, -pocket);

// Peg: a block to seat in the pocket, currently sitting off to the side.
peg = box(14.0, -6.0, 3.0, 26.0, 6.0, 11.0);

return bracket, peg;
